                      (    forth6809.asm):16215                      ; "girl" and replaced only that span, leaving surrounding
                      (    forth6809.asm):16216                      ; "%...%" delimiters untouched in the output - and never
                      (    forth6809.asm):16217                      ; returned the substitution count ANS requires as a
                      (    forth6809.asm):16218                      ; third stack item. Per the ANS spec (forth-standard.org/
                      (    forth6809.asm):16219                      ; standard/string/SUBSTITUTE), SUBSTITUTE must scan for
                      (    forth6809.asm):16220                      ; text between '%' (ASCII $25) delimiter pairs
                      (    forth6809.asm):16221                      ; specifically: "%%" collapses to a single '%' (count
                      (    forth6809.asm):16222                      ; unchanged); a name matching the REPLACES registration
                      (    forth6809.asm):16223                      ; has the ENTIRE "%name%" span - delimiters included -
                      (    forth6809.asm):16224                      ; replaced by the substitution text (count incremented);
                      (    forth6809.asm):16225                      ; a non-matching name is passed through unchanged,
                      (    forth6809.asm):16226                      ; delimiters and all (count unchanged); an unpaired
                      (    forth6809.asm):16227                      ; trailing '%' with no closing delimiter passes the
                      (    forth6809.asm):16228                      ; residue through unchanged. Confirmed via MAME testing
                      (    forth6809.asm):16229                      ; against a real template. GLOBALS is fully packed
