                      (    forth6809.asm):16447                                  ; testing whatever flags an unrelated, earlier
                      (    forth6809.asm):16448                                  ; instruction happened to leave set, not the
                      (    forth6809.asm):16449                                  ; sign of the value just popped. TSTA
                      (    forth6809.asm):16450                                  ; explicitly tests D's high byte immediately
                      (    forth6809.asm):16451                                  ; before the branch that depends on it. The
                      (    forth6809.asm):16452                                  ; four existing internal callers (DOT/DOTR/
                      (    forth6809.asm):16453                                  ; DDOT/DDOTR, i.e. . / .R / D. / D.R) were
                      (    forth6809.asm):16454                                  ; accidentally unaffected - each happens to
                      (    forth6809.asm):16455                                  ; run "LDD SAVEN" (a flag-setting load of the
                      (    forth6809.asm):16456                                  ; true signed value) immediately before PSHU
                      (    forth6809.asm):16457                                  ; D/JSR SIGN, and PSHU doesn't disturb flags -
                      (    forth6809.asm):16458                                  ; but this was fragile, caller-side luck, not
                      (    forth6809.asm):16459                                  ; SIGN being correct on its own. Confirmed via
                      (    forth6809.asm):16460                                  ; MAME: a direct, standalone use of SIGN (not
                      (    forth6809.asm):16461                                  ; preceded by an unrelated flag-setting
                      (    forth6809.asm):16462                                  ; instruction) never added the minus sign for
                      (    forth6809.asm):16463                                  ; either sign of input.
